WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.709 --> 00:00:04.250
We all have goals in life.

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:06.020
Some are short term.

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:07.470
Some are long term.

00:00:07.470 --> 00:00:15.730
But what is the motivation out of which we
create and pursue these goals?

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:22.470
The reason we create goals in life is to create
and sustain a sense of motion.

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:29.170
Without feeling like we are moving towards
something, we feel useless and uninspired

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:33.440
and experience an existential lethargy.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:38.929
We need goals to feel engaged and connected
to the natural world.

00:00:38.929 --> 00:00:45.600
Every goal you set in life is ultimately a
goal of nature and evolution.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:52.980
Even the most individualistic seeming of goals
are primed by some desire to benefit the collective

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:54.130
life around you.

00:00:54.130 --> 00:01:01.199
You are a part of nature’s progression,
and if you wish to feel alive and a part of

00:01:01.199 --> 00:01:07.540
the system of existence, you must move forward
with it.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:14.390
Experiencing and participating in the collective
forward motion of life is essential, but we

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:22.210
must also be careful to not become so swept
away by it that we forget to also enjoy our

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:24.909
individual lives.

00:01:24.909 --> 00:01:31.560
We must learn the balance between actively
working towards and pursuing our goals, while

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:36.430
still being able to enjoy our life around
them.

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:43.740
Our sense of identity and self-worth do not
have to be attached exclusively to the cycle

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:46.640
of goal-oriented success.

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:51.909
The cycle being; goal-task-accomplishment-repeat.

00:01:51.909 --> 00:01:58.640
This cycle infinitely regresses on itself,
and searching for our overall wellbeing within

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:02.650
it will only leave us empty handed.

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:09.360
True wellbeing comes from enjoying and being
motivated towards goals, while not solely

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:15.070
depending on them for a sense of enjoyment
and self-worth.

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:23.330
When your goals become your only lifeline
to life itself, you bring anxiety, desperation,

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:27.250
risk-aversion, and fear into them.

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:34.130
It is important to be motivated and passionate
about the outcome of your goals, but the paradox

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:41.130
is not being so overly dependent on them that
you forget to enjoy them and take risks to

00:02:41.130 --> 00:03:06.390
develop them.

